wineserver: index a process's memory views by base address as well.

Wine's server keeps a process's views in a list and walks it on every map
and unmap request. VIctory-macOS #155 reports the title mapping and
unmapping 64 KiB views thousands of times a frame, at about 1 ms a request
with about 20,000 views mapped (WineHQ bug 60868). With the views also in a
red-black tree by base, find_mapped_view, find_mapped_addr and
is_valid_view_addr are O(log n). No protocol change.

By UwUCammie, posted in fxceless/victory-fork#184 against Wine 11.22. It
applies to CrossOver 26.3.0's Wine 11.0 unchanged. One line added here:
add_view_to_tree clears view->tree first, so a view the tree refuses
(a base already in it, which cannot happen while views do not overlap)
never leaves mem_alloc's garbage there for free_memory_view to remove.

Like Wine, this patch is under the LGPL 2.1 or later. Applied by
tools/macos/build-crossover-wine.sh.

